WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.480
In the Tenderloins' haste to be hilarious
and bust each other's chops in stunts and

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.860
punishments, the titular Impractical Jokers
can get, well… carried away.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:15.400
The kooky antics of Q, Murr, Joe, and Sal
can and do veer into the unseemly, dangerous,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.760
or even illegal, as these extreme examples
demonstrate.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.840
A very special 2014 episode featured maybe
the most extreme punishment yet, and one that

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:29.410
would be hard to top, as it involved parties
outside of the Impractical Jokers foursome

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.760
as well as the government and what's likely
a great deal of paperwork.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.320
Jenna Vulcano is a recurring Impractical Jokers
cast member, showing up whenever her brother

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.560
Sal needs to be made especially uncomfortable
by his cronies.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:44.680
Her appearances usually involve staging some
kind of intimate encounter with the three

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.140
Jokers that aren't Sal.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.800
The third season finale "Brother-in-Loss"
tops them all.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.070
Sal lost the episode, and for his punishment
he had to watch, alongside his family and

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.800
friends, as Murr married Jenna.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.300
That's really going above and beyond, and
the duo really did tie the knot, however briefly.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.680
In fact, following this matrimonial episode,
Murr even tweeted:

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.740
"Yes I legally married Sal's sister, no joke.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.760
And yes we annulled the marriage... after
the honeymoon night!"

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:14.080
Dental procedures are among life's most unpleasant
and potentially painful things, so even the

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.460
idea of delving into that world as part of
an otherwise innocuous and silly prank show

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.700
feels a bit beyond the pale.

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:25.180
And yet, on a 2014 episode of Impractical
Jokers, the Tenderloins made Murr, a man purported

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:29.840
to be their friend, submit to some unnecessary
and deeply uncomfortable oral treatment for

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.580
his punishment, having lost the episode.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.799
Because the dental anesthetic of novocaine
is a powerful numbing agent, it's inherently

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.240
funny to listen to somebody try use the mouth
they cannot feel, not to mention try to eat

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:40.800
food.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:45.180
Murr thus endured some novocaine shots and
then had to talk about a variety of foods

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.420
while also eating them.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:47.640
"Braised beef…"

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.240
"Braised beef…" "...is brilliant."

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:56.120
"...is… braised b… braised beef is b…"

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.240
In short, he made a terrible mess.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.009
The bit had long-lasting implications for
Murr, too.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.659
Responding to an Impractical Jokers fan on
Twitter, Murr revealed that since the novocaine-related

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.720
punishment he's now, quote, "more sensitive
to it."

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.600
Complicating future dental surgeries now that's
suffering for one's art.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:18.020
"The Permanent Punishment," the title of a
2014 Impractical Jokers episode, is also,

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.390
unfortunately for three Jokers, a spoiler.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.660
In a prank involving attaching balloons onto
people just trying to grocery shop, Q, Murr,

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.010
and Sal in other words, everyone except Joe
fails, and gets their punishment.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:33.530
For each guy it's a possibly eternal reminder
of that time they didn't succeed on their

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:35.160
silly reality show: a tattoo.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.190
The Jokers go under the needle and ink to
receive the worst and dumbest tattoos this

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:40.290
side of Jackass.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.790
Q's consists of a cat, along with the caption
"38.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.790
Lives Alone.

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.400
Has 3 Cats."

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:50.400
That's mildly embarrassing, but not as ridiculous
and pointless as Murr's sweet body art depicting

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.660
a ferret skydiving.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.820
Again, that's funny and humiliating for Murr,
but the hardest, weirdest, and silliest permanent

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.520
ink of all went onto poor Sal.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.780
Because rules are rules and punishments must
be accepted on Impractical Jokers, he got

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.580
a thigh tattoo of musician, actor, and celebrity
offspring Jaden Smith.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:11.200
And let's be honest it's not even a particularly
lifelike likeness of the rising star, either.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:16.900
The Impractical Joker who loses this 2015
episode is once again Sal, and his co-stars

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:20.410
select a deceptively simple though no less
humiliating punishment.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:24.360
The group heads to a New Jersey escape room
place called Exit Strategy and makes Sal go

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.270
through the experience get locked in a room
and solve riddles to get out with a group

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.120
of strangers.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.400
But going through this mildly entertaining
group outing is not the entirety of the punishment

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.120
Sal has to pee his pants while locked in this
small, enclosed space with other people.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:41.930
Urinating on oneself falls well outside of
the box of what's considered normal and acceptable

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:46.730
adult behavior, but Sal is faced with having
to fake a bathroom emergency, then make the

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.570
problem, well… rectify itself.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:53.050
He literally starts to sweat, and the others
try to force his hand or bladder by playing

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.120
running water sounds through his earpiece.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.030
Finally, Sal does what he has to do and urinates
in full view of everyone, in the escape room,

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.300
fully staining his lightly-colored khakis.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.350
It so freaks out his unwitting escape room
companions that some scream and some can't

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.220
help but laugh.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:11.040
But he still can't get out of the room until
a solution can be found, forcing pee-soaked

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.740
Sal to work in close contact with these strangers.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.320
"That was awesome!"

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.480
"Don't — no, don't touch me!"

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.880
Murr and Joe lost a 2014 Impractical Jokers
episode, leaving them to a punishment called

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:24.640
"Strip High Five."

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:29.200
Both would stand in New York City's Union
Square and ask pedestrians for high fives.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.400
Every time they're refused, the Joker must
remove an article of clothing, and the punishment

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.990
is over when one of them winds up completely
naked.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.900
An onscreen graphic reveals that Sal and Q
almost replaced the punishment because they

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:44.100
thought getting high fives would be too easy
for Murr and Joe, and thus nobody would get

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:44.600
nude.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.780
At first, it looks like that instinct was
correct, as the two easily get strangers to

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.800
slap their palms.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.100
Then the goodwill of their fellow humans dries
up, and both Murr and Joe are forced to remove

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.960
more and more, with Joe losing both his shirt
and pants before his opponent.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.200
Adding insult to injury, Murr's discarded
sweatshirt gets swiped by a rude stranger.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.340
"Oh, no!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.340
Jojo…"

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:06.700
"This is a rough one!"

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:14.140
The battle goes down to the wire, with both
guys left in their underwear and Murr ultimately

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:14.640
losing.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.260
It takes him a good three minutes to steel
himself for the demeaning and illegal act

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.139
of exposing himself in front of the gathered
crowd.

00:05:21.139 --> 00:05:24.169
And that's when New York City police arrive
and put an end to the shoot.

00:05:24.169 --> 00:05:28.240
They didn't arrest anybody, but they most
certainly could have, as exposing one's private

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.300
parts on a street is quite illegal.

